1
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone short on cash, come to my place.

2
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,980
I'm broke too, but don't worry.

3
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:36,100
Look at the blue sky, the white clouds.

4
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,900
Stop right there! Thieves, Inc.!

5
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:02,420
Thief!

6
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:06,120
Stop!

7
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:13,140
Another purse-snatcher?

8
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:15,700
That's the eighth one this week, isn't it?

9
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:18,640
And they keep happening one
after another in our jurisdiction.

10
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:21,920
At this rate, we'll be seen as incompetent.

11
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:23,460
We already are, I'd say.

12
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:27,440
What are they planning,
taking photos of the culprit and the victim?

13
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:29,320
It seems like nothing but bad taste.

14
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:31,310
Speaking of hobbies, Ryo-san,

15
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:34,500
did you go pick up that thing
the Chief asked you to get?

16
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:37,100
I forgot!

17
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:43,040
Take care, and give my regards to Mr. Ohara.

18
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:46,500
I can't believe the Chief would
pay 300,000 yen for this junk.

19
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:46,920
Thank you very much.

20
00:02:48,820 --> 00:02:51,080
I'm hungry.

21
00:02:52,160 --> 00:02:53,927
At this rate,
I can't even afford a beef bowl,

22
00:02:53,977 --> 00:02:56,400
I just have to hang on until Friday.

23
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:03,020
Shichiya.

24
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:06,980
If I pawn this at Shichiya,

25
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:13,160
No, no, this is Chief Ohara's precious

26
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:18,100
But needs must when the devil drives.

27
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:21,820
No, not that,
because this belongs to the Chief.

28
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:24,940
The Chief won't be back until
the day after tomorrow, right?

29
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:26,120
Uh-oh.

30
00:03:34,980 --> 00:03:36,540
So, how much can you lend me?

31
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:43,720
Ten thousand yen, that's about it.

32
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:45,200
What, ten thousand yen?

33
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:48,080
You see, this was in the shop right over there
until just now.

34
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:50,380
This is an item that
was priced at 300,000 yen!

35
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:53,020
Sure, the craftsmanship is good, though.

36
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:58,940
I can only lend ten thousand.
If you don't like that, let's call it off.

37
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:05,340
Cheapskate. But with ten thousand yen,
I can get more yakiniku

38
00:04:06,260 --> 00:04:17,320
Borrow ten thousand, eat yakiniku. Tomorrow, when I get paid, pay back the money and retrieve this.
The day after tomorrow, when the Chief returns from his trip, hand over the scroll. All good.

39
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:19,000
Deal.

40
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:29,160
Damn, I'm in that photo too!

41
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:30,360
Stop!

42
00:04:35,260 --> 00:04:36,880
Damn, they're cutting us off!

43
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:45,140
Alright, up ahead is a left
curve on a one-way street.

44
00:04:45,140 --> 00:04:46,740
I won't let him get away.

45
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:50,160
Alright, 3, 2, 1!

46
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,520
No way, the car just vanished!

47
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:12,380
A task force has been
set up at headquarters,

48
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:15,080
so it's only a matter of time
before the culprit is caught.

49
00:05:16,260 --> 00:05:19,900
We have to get that scroll
back before the Chief sees it.

50
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:22,460
The crime scene is in
front of Nanaya-san's place.

51
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:25,160
Ryo-chan, what was Nanaya-san doing?

52
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:29,580
What kind of patrol is this?
No matter how you look at it,

53
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:33,340
Ryo-san, you went to retrieve the
scroll the Chief asked for, right?

54
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:35,900
What about the scroll?

55
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:37,740
The scroll?

56
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:42,980
Don't tell me, senpai,
you pawned the Chief's hanging scroll?

57
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:45,280
Well, it was closed, you see.

58
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:47,800
The shop was closed,
so I couldn't go back and get it.

59
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:53,480
And on my way home there was a pawnshop, so I just
took a peek, thinking there might be a good find.

60
00:05:54,460 --> 00:05:55,680
I see. So that's what happened.

61
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:56,540
I'm relieved.

62
00:05:56,540 --> 00:06:01,460
Right, pawning someone else's things is what a thief would do,
isn't it?

63
00:06:01,460 --> 00:06:04,880
As if I would ever do something like that.

64
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:12,060
Uh-oh. This is really, really bad.

65
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,460
What? It was open until just now, wasn't it?

66
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:21,240
Give me back the scroll, please.

67
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:23,980
Hey! Hey!

68
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:30,080
Let's say we get the scroll back tomorrow...

69
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:31,480
The photo!

70
00:06:32,740 --> 00:06:34,840
I have to get that photo back, at least.

71
00:06:39,620 --> 00:06:41,100
Kameari 2-chome intersection

72
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:43,500
Motorcycle and passenger
car collision reported

73
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:46,480
Isn't it bad to act on our
own and outsmart headquarters?

74
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:48,920
We don't have time for such leisurely talk.

75
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:53,940
Purse-snatching near the
Aoto 6-chome intersection

76
00:06:53,940 --> 00:06:56,300
Red passenger car, Kanna-nana, heading north

77
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,000
We're in trouble, hurry!

78
00:06:59,000 --> 00:06:59,940
Alright, got it.

79
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:11,080
There he is!

80
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:12,720
Don't let him get away!

81
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:13,880
Leave it to me.

82
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:27,560
Aaaaah!

83
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:30,480
Ryo-san!

84
00:07:34,060 --> 00:07:34,940
It's gone.

85
00:07:34,940 --> 00:07:36,660
Damn it, not again.

86
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:39,480
This is such a pain.

87
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:40,240
Let's go, Honda.

88
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,420
Roger.

89
00:07:48,300 --> 00:07:49,640
What do we do, boss?

90
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:50,160
Mm.

91
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:58,180
Hah!

92
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:01,880
Hah!

93
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:04,620
Look! We have to follow that trailer!

94
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:05,920
Roger!

95
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:13,000
I'll let you wait on
standby until I contact you!

96
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:14,040
Vroom!

97
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:15,660
Biker gang!

98
00:08:19,260 --> 00:08:20,760
Alright! I won't let them get away!

99
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:34,040
Looks like they've finally
reached their hideout.

100
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:40,800
Honestly.

101
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:43,580
Our section chief is a real slave driver

102
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:46,340
Holiday overtime is going to kill me.

103
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:50,300
I wish we'd get a new recruit, at least.

104
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:53,120
Section chief? New recruit?

105
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:55,260
Get one for me too.

106
00:08:59,140 --> 00:09:01,380
Guess I misjudged you

107
00:09:03,340 --> 00:09:04,000
Bingo!

108
00:09:16,340 --> 00:09:17,920
Where did those two go?

109
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:19,240
Whoa, sorry!

110
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:21,400
You're the new employees, right?

111
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:23,160
The conference room is this way.

112
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:24,200
No, well...

113
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:30,360
These are our sales results
for the past six months.

114
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:35,020
Damn it.

115
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:42,040
As you can see, the Purse-Snatching Section's results
have been trending downward for the past half year or so.

116
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:43,520
Purse-Snatching Section?

117
00:09:44,140 --> 00:09:48,680
Along with the Pilfering Section, it's
becoming a burden on our Thief Co., Ltd.

118
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,460
Thief Co., Ltd.?

119
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:57,840
At this rate, we won't make it through the March
fiscal year-end or the June shareholders' meeting.

120
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:01,400
Thieves.

121
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:04,060
Brazenly putting up a sign and everything.

122
00:10:06,180 --> 00:10:08,640
Lately, tardiness and early
departures have been noticeable.

123
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:11,220
Everyone, tighten up and
apply yourselves to your duties.

124
00:10:11,220 --> 00:10:11,680
Yes.

125
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:13,780
It's those two.

126
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:16,540
Your report for today...

127
00:10:16,940 --> 00:10:17,660
Yes, Section Chief.

128
00:10:22,540 --> 00:10:23,920
Haven't seen you before, have you?

129
00:10:24,780 --> 00:10:28,960
Nice to meet you. We've been assigned here from today,
so please take care of us.

130
00:10:30,540 --> 00:10:34,880
I see, glad you came. It's the end of the fiscal year and we could use every hand,
so I'm counting on you.

131
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:37,380
Yes, let's do our best together.

132
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:41,320
Nice to meet you. Nice to meet you all, too.

133
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:46,740
Fasten your uniform properly,
all the way up to the top button.

134
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:50,480
And in our line of work,
being able to run away fast is everything.

135
00:10:51,460 --> 00:10:52,240
Go to the General Affairs Section.

136
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:54,160
Get yourself a pair of good shoes.

137
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:56,340
No, I'm fine with these sandals,

138
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:57,640
since they're my trademark.

139
00:10:58,100 --> 00:10:59,360
No, no, that won't do.

140
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:01,200
Now that you've become part of our company,

141
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:03,260
behavior that disturbs
the company's discipline

142
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:04,200
you'll have to refrain from.

143
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:07,480
Even though you're constantly
disturbing public morals yourself,

144
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:08,820
Did you say something?

145
00:11:08,820 --> 00:11:10,100
No, nothing at all.

146
00:11:10,700 --> 00:11:11,760
Anyway,

147
00:11:11,760 --> 00:11:13,760
I have a question.

148
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:15,780
Now, everyone,

149
00:11:15,780 --> 00:11:18,220
we're going to take photos of
you at your workplace, right?

150
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:19,720
Why?

151
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:21,040
This here,

152
00:11:21,460 --> 00:11:25,160
this is a photo to prove that you did it,
without a doubt.

153
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:28,980
We'll use these records
to assess your salaries.

154
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:32,480
Salary? Even though we're thieves,
we get paid a salary?

155
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:34,440
Because this is a company, after all.

156
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:36,540
You, take this to accounting.

157
00:11:36,540 --> 00:11:37,080
Yes, sir.

158
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:40,700
That's not all.

159
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:42,780
Twice-yearly bonuses

160
00:11:42,780 --> 00:11:43,920
Company trips

161
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:46,880
Our generous benefits
package is our company's pride.

162
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:49,060
Wow, it's just like a regular company!

163
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:51,060
So this is Thief Co., Ltd.

164
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:55,080
If we rake in everything in this range,
a bonus raise won't be just a dream!

165
00:11:55,460 --> 00:11:57,300
I'll do my best!

166
00:11:57,580 --> 00:11:58,000
Mm!

167
00:11:58,180 --> 00:11:59,400
By the way, Section Chief!

168
00:11:59,740 --> 00:12:02,060
What was your specialty originally?

169
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:04,800
I'm a top-notch swindler!

170
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:05,660
Just as I thought.

171
00:12:05,660 --> 00:12:06,360
Let's do our best!

172
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:24,780
Senpai, maybe they're beating the
crap out of you right about now.

173
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:26,960
Right, with this -

174
00:12:33,060 --> 00:12:35,540
Don't go calling me like that!

175
00:12:35,540 --> 00:12:38,000
Thank goodness, you're safe, Senpai.

176
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,340
We were worried about you.

177
00:12:39,340 --> 00:12:41,360
Where are you right now?

178
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:44,620
Or maybe I've stumbled into
some seriously dangerous place.

179
00:12:45,420 --> 00:12:48,140
What? I can't hear you very well.

180
00:12:49,180 --> 00:12:51,060
Doronko stock trading?

181
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:53,320
Close, but not quite.

182
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:55,560
Anyway, just stand by.

183
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:57,620
Once we get a handle on the
gang's specific movements,

184
00:12:57,620 --> 00:12:59,420
I'll contact you, got it?

185
00:13:01,100 --> 00:13:02,400
While we're at it,
scouting out the enemy camp,

186
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:04,560
we have to get that scroll back.

187
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:06,140
What about accounting?

188
00:13:08,640 --> 00:13:09,960
Hey, did you hear?

189
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:12,100
Apparently Akisuka's section
chief is being transferred.

190
00:13:12,100 --> 00:13:13,000
No way!

191
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:16,420
Apparently the marriage-scam prince
is retiring by year's end too.

192
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:17,180
That's shocking.

193
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:18,960
And I had my eye on him!

194
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:20,820
Izuko's the same scenery too

195
00:13:22,180 --> 00:13:23,240
Here it is.

196
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:24,080
There you are!

197
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:28,360
The practical training for new hires is starting,
so please hurry.

198
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:29,160
Practical training

199
00:13:32,180 --> 00:13:34,220
100 yen, 200 yen

200
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:37,780
Once I've counted the coins, 3, 4...

201
00:13:37,780 --> 00:13:39,760
Asking the soba shop owner for the time

202
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:40,640
What time is it now?

203
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:42,580
Then the shop owner says,

204
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:44,240
"It's five o'clock."

205
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:46,060
6, 7...

206
00:13:46,060 --> 00:13:46,520
Hey!

207
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:47,520
Thanks for your business!

208
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:50,500
It's a neat trick to
pocket an extra 100 yen.

209
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:57,460
What secret trick? That's just the soba-noodle scam from the rakugo story
"Toki Soba"!

210
00:13:57,460 --> 00:14:01,140
Even kids today wouldn't
fall for a trick like that.

211
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:02,040
Did you say something?

212
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:05,380
Wow, I didn't notice at all!

213
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:07,840
Okay, hide.

214
00:14:10,020 --> 00:14:12,360
Your stomach is showing. Pull it in.

215
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:14,500
Alright, OK. Next, this one.

216
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:16,420
Your butt.

217
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:21,720
If you can't hide anywhere, you won't
last as an employee of our company.

218
00:14:22,620 --> 00:14:23,860
Belly, belly!

219
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:25,980
Okay, next, this.

220
00:14:28,140 --> 00:14:29,060
I can do it!

221
00:14:40,020 --> 00:14:41,540
Okay, all done.

222
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:45,500
What is this getup,
looking like a thief from ages ago?

223
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:48,080
It's our company's night-shift uniform.

224
00:14:49,940 --> 00:14:51,460
That'll only make you stand out more!

225
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:04,920
Senpai, hello? Senpai!

226
00:15:04,920 --> 00:15:06,560
Hello, hello, hello, hello!

227
00:15:09,580 --> 00:15:11,180
Where are we going now?

228
00:15:11,180 --> 00:15:12,760
Newbies start out on lookout duty.

229
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:14,440
Just follow me quietly.

230
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:15,960
Don't worry about it.

231
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:17,740
You'll get the knack of it in no time.

232
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:20,860
We need to boost our
performance around here.

233
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:22,920
It's dangerous, you know.

234
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:25,040
The company seems to be
struggling financially, too.

235
00:15:25,040 --> 00:15:27,380
Even if I ask a basic question...

236
00:15:28,540 --> 00:15:28,940
What?

237
00:15:29,580 --> 00:15:30,540
If you're a thief,

238
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:33,220
speak up loud enough for me to hear.

239
00:15:33,220 --> 00:15:37,480
Wouldn't a thief earn more working alone?

240
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:39,840
Why a company?

241
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:43,220
Half-baked thieves like us,

242
00:15:43,220 --> 00:15:45,460
this trade isn't easy
enough to survive in alone.

243
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:48,340
These days,
the world is dangerous, you know.

244
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:50,420
Small-time crooks like us

245
00:15:50,420 --> 00:15:52,320
have to huddle together to get by.

246
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:54,940
You can't make a living on your own either,

247
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:56,520
so you joined our company, didn't you?

248
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:59,140
Well, it just sort of happened.

249
00:15:59,140 --> 00:16:01,160
They say you reap what you sow.

250
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:06,680
Newcomer.

251
00:16:06,680 --> 00:16:08,260
You stay here

252
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:09,700
if you see anyone suspicious,

253
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:11,440
signal us with this.

254
00:16:12,020 --> 00:16:12,660
Understood.

255
00:16:14,100 --> 00:16:15,720
We're the suspicious ones here, you know!

256
00:16:16,460 --> 00:16:17,460
Sound the siren

257
00:16:17,460 --> 00:16:19,440
and come to the rental warehouse in Block 4.

258
00:16:20,420 --> 00:16:21,600
Don't we need to let them know?

259
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:22,920
Not yet, it's too early.

260
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:25,560
When we catch them,
we'll get them all in one sweep.

261
00:16:25,980 --> 00:16:27,520
How is it? Just a little more.

262
00:16:28,260 --> 00:16:29,080
Hurry up.

263
00:16:29,080 --> 00:16:31,280
No, it's a state-of-the-art lock, it seems.

264
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:33,680
Emergency call, emergency call!

265
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:34,500
Whoa, what happened?

266
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:38,180
Suspicious figures are
loitering around the truck.

267
00:16:38,180 --> 00:16:39,560
What should we do?

268
00:16:39,740 --> 00:16:41,220
Got it, I'm on my way.

269
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:43,200
Once it opens, haul everything out fast.

270
00:16:49,680 --> 00:16:50,660
What the heck is this?

271
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:54,620
Five or six men in sunglasses
and black suits suddenly

272
00:16:54,620 --> 00:16:58,380
I bet those guys are from Thief Co., Ltd.!

273
00:16:58,380 --> 00:17:00,180
Is there really such a thing?

274
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:02,940
We can't just stand here.
Hurry and put it back!

275
00:17:03,780 --> 00:17:05,000
What happened here?

276
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:06,180
Sorry.

277
00:17:06,180 --> 00:17:09,360
Weren't we supposed to be
a snatch-and-grab outfit?

278
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:11,340
Since we have so few employees here,

279
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,720
Stop wasting your breath
and keep carrying these out!

280
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:18,660
Newcomer, you go along too!

281
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:21,640
Is the Honda still not here?

282
00:17:26,100 --> 00:17:28,020
A patrol car! It's the white plum!

283
00:17:29,020 --> 00:17:30,680
Can't be helped. Back to the car.

284
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:32,160
Rookies, go earn some money!

285
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:34,320
Your right foot's quicker.

286
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:36,060
This guy has really poor prospects.

287
00:17:37,220 --> 00:17:38,800
Zero results today.

288
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:41,620
Idiot man!

289
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:45,280
Of all things,
leaving the car right at the scene!

290
00:17:45,280 --> 00:17:47,160
A written apology won't be enough, you know.

291
00:17:47,160 --> 00:17:49,760
Everyone to the scene, to the scene!

292
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:59,120
If our pay gets cut any more,
we won't be able to eat.

293
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:03,000
Exactly.
We haven't been paid in three months.

294
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:06,660
Bonuses are postponed,
and company trips are a pipe dream.

295
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:09,360
I figured as much.

296
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:13,660
If we don't hit a big score soon,
we'll all dry up and starve!

297
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:16,080
There's talk like that.

298
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:20,040
A huge project involving the whole
company is underway at the top.

299
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:24,040
Senpai.

300
00:18:25,660 --> 00:18:26,960
That's unreasonable!

301
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:31,220
We'll catch Thief Number One red-handed!

302
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:33,540
This is a once-in-a-lifetime chance!

303
00:18:34,860 --> 00:18:35,760
Hey, you there.

304
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:38,920
Once I know the details of the plan,
I'll get back to you.

305
00:18:40,020 --> 00:18:42,540
Hello? Ryo-chan, we got cut off.

306
00:18:42,540 --> 00:18:46,000
Charging into enemy territory alone is way too cool,
you know.

307
00:18:46,380 --> 00:18:48,620
Maybe we should contact
headquarters after all.

308
00:18:48,620 --> 00:18:49,060
Yeah.

309
00:18:50,080 --> 00:18:53,120
So the underground tunnel to
Kameari Bank is finished, then.

310
00:18:54,020 --> 00:18:55,340
Yes, everything is ready.

311
00:18:55,340 --> 00:18:56,140
But...

312
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:57,100
What's wrong?

313
00:18:57,100 --> 00:18:59,960
Security is tight right now, too.

314
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:03,740
Shouldn't we postpone and
wait for things to cool down?

315
00:19:03,740 --> 00:19:05,420
If you keep talking like that, so casually,

316
00:19:05,420 --> 00:19:07,260
our company is going to go bankrupt!

317
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:09,580
To do it or not to do it...

318
00:19:09,580 --> 00:19:12,620
Let's do it.

319
00:19:13,900 --> 00:19:15,080
We absolutely must do it.

320
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:17,220
With the whole company,
all the employees together,

321
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:19,180
if we're going to get
through the March settlement,

322
00:19:19,180 --> 00:19:21,460
let's make this project a success.

323
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:23,960
What are you talking about?

324
00:19:23,960 --> 00:19:25,780
This is no place for newcomers.

325
00:19:25,780 --> 00:19:26,840
That enthusiasm is good.

326
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:30,260
I want to make up for today's failure.

327
00:19:30,260 --> 00:19:32,400
Thorough preparation, all set.

328
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:33,480
Kenbō Jūsaku

329
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:35,020
That's fine too.

330
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:38,740
But in the end, it's passion for one's work.

331
00:19:38,740 --> 00:19:39,560
It's passion.

332
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:41,560
It's the feeling of wanting to move forward.

333
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:43,820
And the hopes of all employees.

334
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:45,360
Our beloved company is our life.

335
00:19:45,360 --> 00:19:48,900
Difficult work is the path we must take.

336
00:19:54,040 --> 00:19:55,200
Wonderful.

337
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:58,280
That Toki Soba old man.

338
00:19:58,760 --> 00:20:00,980
The biggest job since
our company was founded.

339
00:20:00,980 --> 00:20:03,140
Let's make our mark here.

340
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:04,480
President.

341
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:08,120
Okay, that's that, all set.

342
00:20:09,740 --> 00:20:11,340
All we need to do is contact them.

343
00:20:12,340 --> 00:20:13,600
Before that...

344
00:20:18,620 --> 00:20:20,600
I brought the apology letter, but...

345
00:20:21,620 --> 00:20:23,080
There's nobody here

346
00:20:25,567 --> 00:20:28,004
the report,

347
00:20:28,054 --> 00:20:29,920
the report.

348
00:20:31,880 --> 00:20:34,000
If we get this, it's ours.

349
00:20:38,080 --> 00:20:39,080
What are you doing?

350
00:20:39,080 --> 00:20:41,140
I brought an apology letter, but...

351
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:45,260
Newbies like you bringing
apology letters to accounting...

352
00:20:45,820 --> 00:20:48,380
You'd better get ready for work instead.

353
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:51,580
Excuse me for the night shift.

354
00:20:57,200 --> 00:21:01,520
One employee is absent due to a cold,
but all the other staff are here, President.

355
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:05,320
Yes, since this is the biggest
job our company has ever undertaken,

356
00:21:05,320 --> 00:21:06,960
everyone, be careful not to get hurt.

357
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:09,700
A job isn't over until
we're back at the company, so

358
00:21:10,340 --> 00:21:12,000
let's do our best and stay energetic!

359
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:15,280
This isn't a school field trip, you know.

360
00:21:15,280 --> 00:21:17,940
Without knowing they'll
all be caught in one net,

361
00:21:18,540 --> 00:21:20,880
Huh?

362
00:21:24,720 --> 00:21:26,740
Without a cell phone,
we can't stay in contact.

363
00:21:27,620 --> 00:21:30,920
If we can't contact each other,
will I be lumped in with the thieves too?

364
00:21:32,980 --> 00:21:34,320
But even trying to escape,

365
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:37,300
why am I at the front?

366
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:40,620
Hang in there, newbie!

367
00:21:40,620 --> 00:21:43,340
Alright, this is what real work is like!

368
00:21:43,340 --> 00:21:46,220
Straight ahead,
charging down the path I believe in...

369
00:21:46,820 --> 00:21:49,640
Listen, my head's starting to spin.

370
00:21:50,120 --> 00:21:51,080
Ow

371
00:21:51,620 --> 00:21:53,760
Why is there a wall here?

372
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:55,520
Alright, we've arrived!

373
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:56,260
Come on.

374
00:21:59,680 --> 00:22:01,480
It's the bank diagonally across the street,
after all.

375
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:06,120
Then there was no need to dig a tunnel like this.
We could've just walked over.

376
00:22:11,960 --> 00:22:15,140
I've finally sunk as low as I possibly can.

377
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:16,480
Kick!

378
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:22,000
We did it, we really did it, President!

379
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:23,260
Aaaaaah!

380
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:33,060
If it's come to this,
I'll take all of these guys on myself -

381
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:34,360
Aaaaaaah!

382
00:22:34,360 --> 00:22:37,080
Aaaaaaah!

383
00:22:37,080 --> 00:22:40,800
Aaaaaaah!

384
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:42,380
Aaaaaaah!

385
00:22:42,380 --> 00:22:43,180
Aaaaaaah!

386
00:22:43,180 --> 00:22:45,700
Aaaaaaah!

387
00:22:45,700 --> 00:22:46,320
Aaaaaaah!

388
00:22:46,320 --> 00:22:49,860
Aaaaaaah!

389
00:22:49,860 --> 00:22:51,340
Aaaaaaah!

390
00:22:51,340 --> 00:22:51,360
Aaaaaaah!

391
00:22:51,360 --> 00:22:52,340
Aaaaaaah!

392
00:22:52,340 --> 00:22:59,460
Aaaaaaah!

393
00:22:59,460 --> 00:23:00,380
Aaaaaaah!

394
00:23:00,380 --> 00:23:01,500
Aaaaaaah!

395
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:04,180
Well, Chief, you're back early.

396
00:23:04,840 --> 00:23:08,840
With the times the way they are, I can't
even relax in a hot spring without worrying.

397
00:23:09,220 --> 00:23:11,340
But how did you find this place?

398
00:23:11,720 --> 00:23:14,540
Headquarters apparently
knew these guys existed too,

399
00:23:14,540 --> 00:23:18,000
but they couldn't decide
when to make a mass arrest.

400
00:23:18,820 --> 00:23:22,680
Thanks to Ryotsu, we got an unexpectedly quick resolution,
and he was really pleased.

401
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:24,720
That's great, senior.

402
00:23:24,720 --> 00:23:28,100
I really respect you, senior.
You're amazing, as always.

403
00:23:28,420 --> 00:23:30,800
Your selfish solo
actions are outrageous, but

404
00:23:30,800 --> 00:23:32,920
this time you did well, Ryotsu.

405
00:23:32,920 --> 00:23:37,180
Being praised even by the Chief
makes me feel kind of itchy.

406
00:23:37,720 --> 00:23:39,540
Senior, you dropped something.

407
00:23:42,380 --> 00:23:43,240
It's a photo, isn't it.

408
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,700
This is the hanging scroll I bought.

409
00:23:47,700 --> 00:23:49,000
Why, to Shishia?

410
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:51,000
Why is Ryotsu receiving money?

411
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:52,840
Explain yourself, Ryotsu.

412
00:23:53,680 --> 00:23:54,560
Ryotsu!

413
00:23:58,100 --> 00:24:00,940
You idiot!

414
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:34,380
That strange feeling I had back then,

415
00:24:35,100 --> 00:24:39,620
so on the tiles of the shopping arcade,

416
00:24:39,620 --> 00:24:45,420
I tried walking only on the black ones.

417
00:24:47,760 --> 00:24:53,680
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten.

418
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:57,700
Politicians with their self-important faces,

419
00:24:57,700 --> 00:25:01,060
and aunties with blue eyeshadow too,

420
00:25:01,060 --> 00:25:04,000
try turning the corner,

421
00:25:04,600 --> 00:25:06,580
that corner there.

422
00:25:07,620 --> 00:25:11,800
You'll meet everyone, everyone.

423
00:25:12,380 --> 00:25:16,320
Over there is Kame-ari,

424
00:25:17,240 --> 00:25:19,720
come on, surely it's Kame-ari!

425
00:25:21,400 --> 00:25:24,960
Come on, everyone, come to our town!

426
00:25:26,180 --> 00:25:26,500
Thank you!

427
00:25:30,500 --> 00:25:33,960
It's Christmas, and I've been
working at a cake shop since morning.

428
00:25:33,960 --> 00:25:35,840
Helping Reiko with her volunteer work,

429
00:25:35,840 --> 00:25:37,900
making a present for the Chief's grandchild,

430
00:25:37,900 --> 00:25:39,640
and coaching Honda on his date.

431
00:25:39,640 --> 00:25:42,240
I've got to get the Tera family
into the amusement park too.

432
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:44,380
At this rate, I'd need several bodies!

433
00:25:44,380 --> 00:25:47,340
Next time:
"Jump Out, Christmas!" See you then!

434
00:25:51,920 --> 00:25:54,160
Surely on camera...

435
00:25:54,160 --> 00:25:59,300
Come on, everyone, come to our town!

436
00:26:00,260 --> 00:26:00,940
Thank you!

